<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Communards</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1871</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Communards were the supporters and defenders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> Commune, the revolutionary government that ruled Paris from March to May 1871. Thousands of them were killed during the 'Bloody Week' of May 1871, when government troops retook the city, and many more were imprisoned or deported to New Caledonia, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louise-michel">Louise Michel</a>. An amnesty allowed the survivors to return in 1880.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/communards.jpg" alt="Communards" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bruno Braquehais · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barricade_Voltaire_Lenoir_Commune_Paris_1871.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
